  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Jacobs Engineering Group obligated $271M in federal contract funding in FY2026 to date. Jacobs Engineering Group received 138 awards for the period, with an average award size of $2M. Jacobs Engineering Group obligations are up 191.9% year over year. Jacobs Engineering Group has shown a multiyear increase in obligations: FY21 were $33.4M, FY22 were $27.5M, FY23 were $52.6M, FY24 were $64M, FY25 were $93M, and FY26 to date are $271M. Jacobs Engineering Group concentration in agencies and markets is clear: the Department of Homeland Security accounts for $151M of FY2026 to date obligations, followed by the Department of Defense at $36.5M and the General Services Administration at $34.1M. Jacobs Engineering Group revenue by NAICS is led by Engineering Services at $245M, with Architectural Services at $14.1M and smaller amounts in Remediation Services and Environmental Consulting Services. The current-year totals are partial and represent contract obligations unless otherwise noted for award-value tables.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the largest federal buyers of Jacobs Engineering Group in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Homeland Security obligated $151M to Jacobs Engineering Group in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense obligated $36.5M and the General Services Administration obligated $34.1M. The Department of Transportation obligated $30.6M and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $14.5M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and services drive Jacobs Engineering Group federal obligations?",
        "body": "Engineering Services is the largest market for Jacobs Engineering Group at $245M in FY2026 to date. Architectural Services provided $14.1M, Remediation Services provided $5.6M, and Environmental Consulting Services provided $5.5M. Jacobs Engineering Group also recorded $1000K in research and development services and smaller amounts in Custom Computer Programming Services ($35.3K)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Jacobs Engineering Group make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Jacobs Engineering Group obligated $271M in federal contract funding in FY2026 to date. Jacobs Engineering Group received 138 awards for the period, with an average award size of $2M, and obligations are up 191.9% year over year. The multiyear obligations show FY21 at $33.4M, FY22 at $27.5M, FY23 at $52.6M, FY24 at $64M, and FY25 at $93M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Jacobs Engineering Group?",
      "a": "The Department of Homeland Security is the largest buyer of Jacobs Engineering Group in FY2026 to date, with $151M in obligations. The Department of Defense obligated $36.5M, the General Services Administration obligated $34.1M, and the Department of Transportation obligated $30.6M. NASA obligated $14.5M and smaller obligations came from EPA ($5.4M), the Department of the Interior ($858K), and the Government Accountability Office ($672K)."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Jacobs Engineering Group sell to the government?",
      "a": "Jacobs Engineering Group sells engineering and related professional services to the government, led by Engineering Services at $245M in FY2026 to date. Jacobs Engineering Group also provided Architectural Services ($14.1M), Remediation Services ($5.6M), Environmental Consulting Services ($5.5M), and research and development services ($1000K), plus smaller amounts in Custom Computer Programming Services ($35.3K)."
    },
